  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n3 ∶ 83\n\n7 ∶ 2403\n\n**Logic: Second no. = [(First no.)⁴ + 2]**\n\n**3 ∶ 83 →**\n\n⇒ [(3)⁴ + 2]\n\n⇒ (81 + 2) = 83\n\n**7 ∶ 2403 →**\n\n⇒ [(7)4 + 2]\n\n⇒ (2401 + 2) = 2403\n\nChecking the given options:\n\n(1) 5 ∶ 629 →\n\n⇒ [(5)4 + 4]\n\n⇒ (625 + 4) = 629\n\n(2) 6 ∶ 1200 →\n\n⇒ [(6)4 - 96]\n\n⇒ (1296 - 96) = 1200\n\n(3) 2 ∶ 18 →\n\n⇒ [(2)4 + 2]\n\n⇒ (16 + 2) = **18**\n\n(4) 4 ∶ 250 →\n\n⇒ [(4)4 + 2]\n\n⇒ (256 - 6) = 250\n\nHere, **'2 : 18' **is similar to the given number pairs.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (3)\".\n\n40:T1123,\n<",
